Welcome to the CheckMate Setup Wizard.\par
\par
CheckMate is released from the DAISY Labs to help explore how AI can help when checking digital publications.\par
\par
This application is an accessible desktop front-end for the DAISY eBraille Checker, W3C EPUBCheck, Ace by DAISY, the W3C Nu HTML Checker, veraPDF, and validators via the DAISY Pipeline (when installed). It lets you open an .ebrl, .epub, .pdf, .html, .svg, or .css file, a DTBook XML or NIMAS/DAISY package, or an exploded publication folder, and see a clear Passed / Passed with warnings / Failed result. .ebrl files are checked with eBraille Checker; .epub files with EPUBCheck and Ace; .pdf files with veraPDF (PDF/UA or PDF/A); .html files with the Nu HTML Checker and axe; .svg and .css with Nu. DAISY 2.02, DAISY 3, DTBook, and NIMAS are checked with validators via a local DAISY Pipeline 2 webservice when it is running.\par
\par
You can also check HTML, CSS, XML, SVG, or MathML copied to the clipboard (File \u8594? Check clipboard\u8230?).\par
\par
On Windows you can right-click an .ebrl, .epub, .pdf, .html, .svg, or .css file and choose "Validate with CheckMate", or use Open with \u8594? CheckMate. On Windows 11 that command is on the classic menu (right-click \u8594? Show more options, or Shift+F10).\par
\par
If Fido is installed with working AI credentials, CheckMate can use that AI to explain issues, suggest fixes, analyse images, and translate to other languages.\par
\par
What this installer includes:\par
  \u8226? CheckMate\par
  \u8226? Bundled Eclipse Temurin Java Runtime (JRE 17)\par
  \u8226? Bundled eBraille Checker\par
  \u8226? Bundled EPUBCheck\par
  \u8226? Bundled Ace by DAISY (with Node.js and Chromium)\par
  \u8226? Bundled veraPDF\par
  \u8226? PyMuPDF (for PDF first-page previews in HTML reports)\par
\par
No separate Java, Node.js, or Ace installation is required. DAISY Pipeline is optional and is not bundled.\par
\par
Click Next to continue.\par
